  {
    "number": 127,
    "title": "Add BUNNY activity and component integration dashboard",
    "body": "BUNNY provides a React/TypeScript interface for shared agent activity, component integration and connection evidence. Nanoleaf and Pixoo controls use the existing hub/controller services, preserve native modes and revision guards, and retain drafts and qualified outcomes across refreshes. Refs #6.\n\nThe dashboard includes scoped context, fixed same-origin assets, memory-only browser credentials, validated editor links and reusable component views. General controls, exact previews, full editor migration, installation and physical operation remain outside this source delivery.\n\nThe user approved UI candidate `a7db5eaa82e14f6f6d9c8f0df50f4220eb174f2a`: \"Approved. The source candidate is approved.\" Frontend source and build script are unchanged in the final candidate. Browser tests now wait for authoritative snapshots between sequential edits. The branch incorporates delivered MCP/setup work and its guide reconciliation, including PRs #126, #128, #129 and #130.\n\nFinal comparison: base/merge-base `012de557257940cc66913c64012cf4d85e13fb91`, head `edfaee750a91cc61549a036b3ac6b4fbccd32a58`. Independent final Standards and Specification reviews have no remaining P0-P2 findings. Both reviewed this exact base/head. Earlier task reviews ran three rounds; seven findings and the surviving partial-receipt refresh defect were corrected with regression evidence. The first final-review CI exposed a test sequencing race; the test now waits for authoritative refresh and its separate conflict assertions remain. The full browser/matrix rerun passed. No check reruns were used to bypass a failure.\n\nLocal validation on Node 24: npm ci, build/type checks, 67 hub tests, reproducible offline package with isolated tests, 5 dashboard unit tests, full browser scenarios and the extended state/accessibility matrix. Browser checks cover explicit commands, mappings and colors, no-write inspection, labels/notices and attributable children, draft/focus preservation, conflicts, slow/offline devices, expired cursors, terminal and uncertain results, partial effects retained after refresh, read-only access and external control. Keyboard and desktop/mobile axe checks pass. Synthetic latency samples remain bounded input for #30, not installed or physical qualification.\n\nOpenSpec `gh-6-unified-dashboard` is synchronized and archived under `2026-09-21-gh-6-unified-dashboard`. Workflow checks pass with 10 specifications, no active changes and 9 archives; all 15 workflow tests pass. The original task 3.3 mixed implementation completion with later delivery gates. Its archive handoff now records completed implementation; final reviews, current-head CI, guarded merge and merged-main checks remain explicit mandatory delivery obligations.\n\nThe guide inputs/output are reconciled with the delivered setup baseline and UI approval. Guide maintenance/browser checks pass. Post-merge history, issue closure and the architecture diagram's delivered dashboard status will be reconciled in a linked guide-only completion PR. Public publication is separate and is not authorized by this source delivery.\n\nDeferred P3 F-STD-2: registered component aliases exactly `activity` or `connections` collide with built-in navigation keys. Ordinary aliases are unaffected; the collision does not bypass permissions or command guards or cause automatic writes. Both final reviewers accepted a nonblocking maintenance deferral. Owner: hub frontend maintenance. The follow-up should use tagged navigation values and cover both aliases.\n\nGitHub protection and ruleset reads return HTTP 403 for the private repository plan. This is unavailable configuration evidence, not proof of absent protection; all procedural checks and the expected-head merge guard remain mandatory.\n\nPending: all six current-head hosted jobs, guarded squash merge, all merged-main jobs, issue closure/readback and guide completion reconciliation. Keep #6 open until merged-main checks pass.\n",
    "state": "open",
